# Fixture sources are tracked; compiled binaries and generated C/LLVM artifacts
# are not. Deny-all plus a small EXTENSION allowlist, which fails SAFE: a new
# fixture at any depth is tracked automatically, while every build output is
# extensionless (`hello`, `driver`) or a .c/.h/.ll/.o — none of which any rule
# below un-ignores, so no re-ignore catch-all is needed.
#
# `!*/` is load-bearing: git will not descend into an excluded directory, so
# directories must be un-ignored before the file rules can match inside them.
*
!*/
!**/*.gg
!**/*.out
!**/*.toml
!**/*.expected
!**/*.txt
!**/*.lock
!**/*.md
!**/*.sh
!.gitignore
